WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.225
Not acting doesn't mean standing still.

2
00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:04.562
It means three things happen by default.

3
00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:07.725
First, money gets spent
without a choice being made.

4
00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:12.837
The BOD 26-02 refresh will
happen on a directive clock.

5
00:00:12.837 --> 00:00:14.738
Run as like-for-like replacement,

6
00:00:14.738 --> 00:00:19.454
the same device class with the same absence
of policy and telemetry, it spends the

7
00:00:19.454 --> 00:00:22.058
money and closes the architecture question

8
00:00:22.058 --> 00:00:24.451
for the service life of the new equipment.

9
00:00:24.451 --> 00:00:26.638
Deferral also has a measured price.

10
00:00:26.638 --> 00:00:33.626
GAO reported in August 2026 that billing
for six agencies' legacy Networx contracts

11
00:00:33.626 --> 00:00:38.019
rose from about 13.4 million
dollars in February 2025

12
00:00:38.019 --> 00:00:42.312
to about 40.9 million in
March, a 206 percent increase.

13
00:00:42.312 --> 00:00:46.724
The book calls that the strongest
cost-of-delay number in the federal record.

14
00:00:46.724 --> 00:00:50.913
Second, gaps surface as findings
rather than accepted risks.

15
00:00:50.913 --> 00:00:56.038
The technical situation is identical either
way; the institutional position isn't.

16
00:00:56.038 --> 00:01:01.311
And cutting managed TIC circuits before
CISA confirms replacement telemetry

17
00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:05.876
trades a gap in transport for a gap
in CISA's visibility, which is worse.

18
00:01:05.876 --> 00:01:08.413
Third, cost gets blamed on the cloud.

19
00:01:08.413 --> 00:01:12.483
When workloads migrate before
transport is governed and measured,

20
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:15.899
slowness is attributed to the
only thing being measured.

21
00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:20.462
The remedies, more instances and
more caching, raise cloud spend.

22
00:01:20.462 --> 00:01:24.353
The book is careful to label
that pattern its own inference,

23
00:01:24.353 --> 00:01:29.275
built on documented parts, so treat it
as a hypothesis to test in your estate.

24
00:01:29.275 --> 00:01:31.325
And one risk sits under all of them.

25
00:01:31.325 --> 00:01:33.412
The governor is attack surface.

26
00:01:33.412 --> 00:01:39.502
In February 2026, Emergency Directive 26-03
ordered action on Cisco SD-WAN systems

27
00:01:39.502 --> 00:01:45.324
after actors were found compromising
them and keeping long-term persistence.

28
00:01:45.324 --> 00:01:48.620
Whatever you buy, protect it
before it carries traffic.
